# The container build must never receive the working tree.
#
# The real capability boundary is the staging directory: the workflow copies an
# allowlisted, manifest-verified Server package plus three named files into
# $RUNNER_TEMP/loom-container-context and builds only that directory — there is
# no `.git`, no source checkout and no credential inside it.
#
# This file is the second line of defence for a manual `docker build .`: exclude
# everything first, then re-include only what the Dockerfile can consume.
*
!docker/
!docker/Dockerfile
!docker/entrypoint.sh
!docker/healthcheck.sh
!scripts/
!scripts/smoke-linux-server.py
!out/
!out/server/
!out/server/linux-x64/
!out/server/linux-x64/**

# Never re-included (no negation may be added for these): .git, _artifacts/,
# root_artifacts/, .oce-client/, node_modules/, target/, dist/, coverage/,
# resources/bin/, mcp-gateway/, docs/prototypes/, .env and .env.*, *.sqlite*,
# *.log, Start-LOOM.cmd, TASK.md, LOG.md, PROJECT_*.md, any credential file.
